tools.description:
Create or replace keyframes on one track, as a single undoable edit. A keyframe at an existing tick is replaced. Each keyframe needs "tick" (or "seconds") plus the fields for the track type:
- CAMERA: {"tick":0,"position":[x,y,z],"yaw":0,"pitch":0,"roll":0} — or "look_at":[x,y,z] instead of yaw/pitch. Same conventions as flashback_set_camera.
- FOV: {"tick":0,"fov":70}
- SPEED: {"tick":0,"speed":0.5} (1 = real time)
- TIME_OF_DAY: {"tick":0,"time":6000} (0-24000; 6000 = noon, 18000 = midnight)
- FREEZE: {"tick":0,"freeze":true,"freezeDelay":0}
- CAMERA_SHAKE: {"tick":0,"frequencyX":1,"amplitudeX":1,"frequencyY":1,"amplitudeY":1}
- CAMERA_ORBIT: {"tick":0,"center":[x,y,z],"distance":10,"yaw":0,"pitch":20}
- TIMELAPSE: {"tick":0,"ticks":0} — "ticks" is the output time at which this replay tick is reached; between two keyframes the replay is sped up to fit.
- TRACK_ENTITY: copy the shape of an existing keyframe from flashback_get_timeline.
Optional "interpolation" on any keyframe sets how the value moves towards the next keyframe: SMOOTH (spline, default), LINEAR, EASE_IN, EASE_OUT, EASE_IN_OUT, HOLD, HERMITE.
A camera path needs at least two CAMERA keyframes; the camera is only driven between the first and last one. Preview with flashback_seek + flashback_screenshot.
